                "reply_count": 6,
                "retweet_count": 8,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "In recognition of #WorldSuicidePreventionDay, I want to urge anyone struggling with their mental health to seek help. \n\nOur military members, law enforcement officers and first responders work hard to keep us safe yet can carry unimaginable burdens from their essential work\u2014and tragically are more likely to die by suicide than in the line of duty. \n\nThe national suicide hotline is 988, and first responders in Florida can find specialized help statewide by calling the Hope Line, 1(866) 4FL-HERO.\n\nIf you need help, don\u2019t delay\u2014caring people are waiting for your call today.",
                "text_lang": "en",
